<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:16:Real Mode">
<!--
    kuna #1288: decompiling a PKLITE-packed DOS executable grew memory without
    bound. Its compressed body decodes as code, and stray 0x4c bytes are
    `DEC SP`.

    `ActionStackPtrFlow`'s `StackSolver` marked an unsolved variable with the
    value 65535 (C++ `coreaction.cc` `StackSolver::propagate`). Equation
    constants are the stack pointer's unsigned offset, so on a 16-bit stack
    pointer `DEC SP` (`SP + 0xffff`) solves to exactly 65535 and reads back as
    unsolved. Here the loop-head MULTIEQUAL, the DEC SP and the call's
    INDIRECT all solve to 65535 and re-pushed each other forever:

        0000  4c           DEC  SP
        0001  e8 0c 00     CALL 0x10
        0004  85 c0        TEST AX,AX
        0006  75 f9        JNZ  0x1
        0008  c3           RET
        0010  c3           RET            ; g
        0011  c2 02 00     RET  2         ; g2

    Where the old solve did finish it still read a real 65535 as unsolved: it
    left that producer unrewritten and the frame offsets past it unsolved. `h`
    reaches entry-1 with PUSH BX after INC SP; it decompiled, but kept a raw
    `char *v3; // sp` local and read its return address through `&v3[-1]`:

        0020  44           INC  SP
        0021  53           PUSH BX        ; SP = entry - 1, solution 65535
        0022  58           POP  AX
        0023  e8 eb ff     CALL 0x11      ; g2 pops 4
        0026  4c           DEC  SP        ; SP = entry + 2
        0027  c3           RET

    Stage: P6 variables, `coreaction_stackptr.rs (StackSolver)`, scheduled in
    `stackstall`. No option: a strict fix, since a solution is now an Option
    and each variable is solved and pushed at most once.

    Assert 1 is the fix: the decompile finishes and prints the loop around
    the call. Before it, this test never finished. Asserts 2 and 3 are `h`:
    its RET reads the slot at entry + 2, and no raw stack-pointer local is
    left (both failed before the fix, with `h` decompiled on its own).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x0">
4ce80c0085c075f9c390909090909090c3c20200909090909090909090909090
445358e8ebff4cc3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x0" name="f"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x10" name="g"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x11" name="g2"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x20" name="h"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu h</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="stacksolver-unsolved #1: the solve terminates and the loop around the call is emitted" min="1" max="1">^  \} while \(g\(\)\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="stacksolver-unsolved #2: h, which terminated before, reads its return address two bytes above the entry slot" min="1" max="1">segment\(v\d+,\*\(unsigned short \*\)segment\(v\d+,&amp;Stack0002\)\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="stacksolver-unsolved #3: no raw stack-pointer local is left" min="0" max="0">// sp$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
